{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778941366,"nonce":"4kCiaTk2PvIrGnXnln00hvrhDpE=","title":"Ledger migration gate: shadow reconciliation and issue API cutover","message":"## Parent\nUmbrella: 097d2b7 — Mandible canonical issue/work ledger with git-bug import/export.\n\nDepends on:\n- ff6a2bc — Ledger core.\n- aac782a — git-bug adapter.\n\n## Scope\nDesign and implement the safe migration path from git-bug-backed issue routes to ledger-backed issue routes without a split-brain window.\n\nThis issue owns:\n- shadow import/reconciliation reports comparing ledger projections against current git-bug scanner output;\n- ambiguous short-ID detection and resolution rules across logical projects;\n- compatibility/fallback mode while ledger data is being validated;\n- selected dual-write or command-gated write strategy where safe;\n- route and CLI cutover plan for existing issue APIs and `mandible issue` commands;\n- rollback plan to scanner-backed reads if reconciliation fails;\n- performance gates for issue list/detail against current scanner behavior.\n\n## Required gates\nDo not switch writes before export/outbox/conflict handling exists. Do not switch reads until reconciliation reports are clean enough on real Mandible corpora.\n\nThe migration should report:\n- issue counts by project/repo;\n- open/closed counts;\n- title/body hash mismatches;\n- label mismatches;\n- comment count/hash mismatches;\n- parent/child relationship mismatches;\n- alias collisions or ambiguous prefixes;\n- auth/work-unit/session link backfill coverage.\n\n## Existing route targets\nCurrent APIs should keep compatibility response shapes where possible:\n- `GET /api/issues`;\n- `GET /api/issues/find/:issueId`;\n- `GET /api/issues/:repoId/:issueId`;\n- comment/status/label mutation endpoints;\n- issue context/spawn endpoints that currently join work units, sessions, auth requests, and branch state.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Implementing the core ledger schema.\n- Implementing the git-bug adapter internals.\n- Graph/UI redesign beyond ensuring APIs expose needed fields.\n\n## Verification\n- Reconciliation tests using fixture corpora.\n- Route tests proving old endpoint shapes remain compatible while backing source changes.\n- Ambiguous alias/prefix tests.\n- Rollback/fallback tests where ledger data is absent or invalid.\n- Performance comparison for issue list/detail routes.\n- Manual smoke on real Mandible issue data before protected-branch submission.\n\n## Done means\nThe project has a controlled, testable path to ledger-backed issue APIs with no window where Mandible writes are invisible to git-bug export, no silent ID collisions, and a documented rollback path.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}